  to rescue Kuma thus the implication is  that they overpowered them in battle or  at least held their own while rescuing  Kuma and retreating considering how much  Oda has hyped up green bull recently  that's insane to think about back in the  day I was disappointed when I found out  that the second in command of the  revolutionaries namely Sabo had a bounty  of only 602 million berries but Oda has  more than made up for it with this  chapter Sabo has actually been  proclaimed the emperor of the Flames AKA  a legendary dog in Pokemon implying he's  taken Luffy's spot as the new fifth  Emperor I mentioned that the spot might  go to someone as well well since we knew  that Luffy would be moving up to yonko  rather than fifth Emperor and I'm so  glad to see it go to Sabo it also makes  revolutionaries look so strong too which  I think they were missing in the past  it's awesome that their second in  command is an emperor and that's not  even to mention their boss Monkey D  Dragon the worst criminal in the world  and then at the end of the chapter akinu  talks to a new character you guys can  speculate as to who you think it is in  the comments but I'm content to let this  detail go for now and I'll Circle back  when we have more information with the  full translated chapter make sure you're  subscribed so you don't miss that and  thank God and Oda that we don't have a  break next week so we won't have to sit  on this bombshell of a chapter for long  without getting any answers smash that  like button if you enjoyed this video  and want to see more like it be a  smashing pirate king and not a passing  Orochi let me know how you enjoy these  chapter spoilers and what you think  you're going to rate this chapter when  it finally comes out in full this has to  be My View From just the spoilers alone  I'm gonna call it right now this has to  be a 10 out of 10. so many crazy moments  and reveals not to mention so many fan  favorite characters coming in in Epic  fashion do n